{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1242598-your-experience-with-larceny-and-thieves","id":1242598,"title":"Your experience with Larceny and thieves?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-03T21:06:31-07:00","id":1242598,"title":"Your experience with Larceny and thieves?","content":"I usually don't like thief type characters in rpgs, because attempting to pickpocket someone becomes a flat roll or two where you are trading instant failure against the chance of gaining a handful of coins, so when I saw Flawless Pickpocketing Technique go out of its way to explicitly say that <i>it is literally impossible to notice,</i> even with magic, I was hooked. The entirety of Larceny is amazing because of how much advantage it gives the proactive user- automatic successes against which only other master charm users can even begin to defend. A charm that lets you cheat several times in a row and get away with it, those bewildered other gamblers unable to pierce the ruse. Smooth talking guards with instantly perceived knowledge. Retconning evidence. All of it is so fantastic. So empowering. It made me really want to play a Larceny supernal.<br /> <br /> How do you guys/girls/Twin faced heroes feel about it? Have you used it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T21:22:04-07:00","id":1242602,"title":"","content":"I have narrated for one such user, and it's pretty interesting.<br /> <br /> It plays excellently to the style of the master thief and the smooth swindler.<br /> It's broadly applicable whenever the characters wanted to interact with any type of underworld, and grandiose to make ocean's 11 moments.<br /> Baiting certain characters into the limelight is easy with it as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T22:01:17-07:00","id":1242613,"title":"","content":"Larceny went from a meh tree to one of my favorites. If you've got a clever player it's a ton of fun to ST for. My game's night caste used it to effectively interrogate an Immaculate monk using Spurious Presence and Preying On Uncertainty","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T22:08:07-07:00","id":1242614,"title":"","content":"Larceny is so, so good. Honestly, with as many moving pieces as there are in 3E, it can be easy to forget how many just outright masterfully flavorful Charms there really are. Larceny is full of them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T06:05:05-07:00","id":1242697,"title":"","content":"Are y\u2019all going to do one of those color-coded rankings for Solar Larceny like others did for Solar Melee and Solar Brawl, to highlight the Must Pick purples from the Please Redesign This reds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T06:58:06-07:00","id":1242704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1242598-your-experience-with-larceny-and-thieves?p=1242697#post1242697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are y\u2019all going to do one of those color-coded rankings for Solar Larceny like others did for Solar Melee and Solar Brawl, to highlight the Must Pick purples from the Please Redesign This reds?</div> </div> </div> </div> No, because I really don't want to bring the crassness of minmax to the superior design of these charms. Larceny is selling a story, building a narrative that Melee or Lore or XYZ isn't. Each step is defining you as a career criminal, a legendary thief. I would hate to sully that with &quot;YMMV but gambling never happens at my table and you cant steal weapons until later like omg wtf charm tax&quot; (Why yes, that IS a nice strawman i built there).<br /> <br /> Besides that, Lareceny is the only time that I felt that Charms <i>challenged</i> me to play their way. Larceny is that person who knows what they are all about and doesn't care if you don't like that. You dont want to gamble, steal, slip through doors, pickpocket from across the room, plant evidence, alter evidence, totally forge a matroshka of identities? then screw off, Larceny isn't for you. It isn't worth taking if you aren't going to get into character, and if you are going to just dip in to fill your concept, then you don't need me or anyone to say &quot;X is good, Y is trash&quot; because your just gonna grab the intro stealing charm and maybe the gambling one and call it a day.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T07:37:41-07:00","id":1242713,"title":"","content":"That's a rather arbitrary decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T08:04:05-07:00","id":1242721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1242598-your-experience-with-larceny-and-thieves?p=1242713#post1242713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a rather arbitrary decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and?<br /> <br /> \u200bBeing asked &quot;Are you going to [do a time-consuming task for no benefit to yourself]?&quot; shouldn't require the answerer to ignore all personal biases; &quot;Because I don't want to&quot; is more than valid as a reply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T08:53:34-07:00","id":1242730,"title":"","content":"As a DM larceny gave me headaches, because I had a player using it constantly for disguises--they supernal'd it for the disguise tree-- and I'm not clever enough to make a sense of danger around a bascially perfect disguise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T09:05:20-07:00","id":1242735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1242598-your-experience-with-larceny-and-thieves?p=1242730#post1242730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a DM larceny gave me headaches, because I had a player using it constantly for disguises--they supernal'd it for the disguise tree-- and I'm not clever enough to make a sense of danger around a bascially perfect disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div>A little off topic but disguises don't work if a character can't keep in line with the role he's playing. There are also cases when you see two people at the same time, one of which would likely have items to prove who he is. Granted a solar can pickpocket them. Though if the person they are trying to disguise is part of a secret society or have methods that only they would know, they could still reveal themselves and force a fight. If you use dragon blooded they should be able to combat it enough to make it not an issue each time. Then there are magic wards and other tools if it's a very sensitive location. That's my two cents on the matter anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T11:17:04-07:00","id":1242758,"title":"","content":"I had a player who picked up Flawless Pickpocketing Technique and went around picking everyone's pockets. It turned into a running joke with the other players, where one of the characters would reach into their pocket to get something and his character would say, &quot;Looking for this?&quot; while holding up whatever it was the character was looking for. His character would play it off, &quot;Oh man, you guys sure are clumsy, always dropping stuff. Good thing thing I'm here, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> Eventually one of the characters got fed up with it so he picked up Flawless Pickpocketing Technique himself just so he could teach the first PC a lesson. But neither of them had terribly good Awareness rolls so they couldn't ever catch one another in the act.<br /> <br /> This led to an amusing scene where they were both picking each other's pockets in the middle of a big fight - &quot;Alright, I throw my pouch full of silver coins at the beastman's head. Oh, did I say <i>my</i> pouch? It's actually your pouch. I picked your pocket last turn.&quot; &quot;Oh that's fine. Your character didn't notice but I stole one of his belts last turn and I'm going to use it as an improvised whip to start whapping the other beastman in the face.&quot;<br /> <br /> By the end of the fight they were both half naked and had strewn one another's gear all across the battlefield.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T18:20:44-07:00","id":1242836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1242598-your-experience-with-larceny-and-thieves?p=1242730#post1242730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a DM larceny gave me headaches, because I had a player using it constantly for disguises--they supernal'd it for the disguise tree-- and I'm not clever enough to make a sense of danger around a bascially perfect disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Allow me to present to you the Holy Trinity:<br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ConfrontingYourImposter?from=Main.BecauseImJonesy\" target=\"_blank\">Because I'm Jonesy</a><br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/IAmOneOfThoseToo\" target=\"_blank\">I am one of those, too</a><br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OutOfCharacterAlert?from=Main.SomethingTheyWouldNeverSay\" target=\"_blank\">Something they would never say</a><br /> <br /> This will help you avoid the inevitable &quot;you've made such a good poisoner that now Captain Antidote is here to thwart you&quot; effect, which really grinds my gears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T21:30:10-07:00","id":1242868,"title":"","content":"My worst experience with Solar Larceny was the Night Caste that was in disguise 24/7. The character was nineteen (I think) and she pretended to be a 40-something male Fire Aspect.<br /> <br /> At no point, in the year that the game went on, did she ever let the other player characters know that she was a Solar or anything. All they knew was her disguise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T05:50:14-07:00","id":1243178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1242598-your-experience-with-larceny-and-thieves?p=1242868#post1242868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My worst experience with Solar Larceny was the Night Caste that was in disguise 24/7. The character was nineteen (I think) and she pretended to be a 40-something male Fire Aspect.<br /> <br /> At no point, in the year that the game went on, did she ever let the other player characters know that she was a Solar or anything. All they knew was her disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way was that bad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T17:56:49-07:00","id":1243346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1242598-your-experience-with-larceny-and-thieves?p=1243178#post1243178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In what way was that bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>The characters never mad a connection to one-another as it was all based on a lie. The player didn't play his character, he played his character's character. It was basically an extra level of detachment which ensured that the character never cared about much of anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T00:33:50-07:00","id":1243424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1242598-your-experience-with-larceny-and-thieves?p=1243346#post1243346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The characters never mad a connection to one-another as it was all based on a lie. The player didn't play his character, he played his character's character. It was basically an extra level of detachment which ensured that the character never cared about much of anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see why that would be frustrating, but I could imagine (depending on the RP skill of the player) that could been extremely cool.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T01:02:34-07:00","id":1243426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1242598-your-experience-with-larceny-and-thieves?p=1242868#post1242868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My worst experience with Solar Larceny was the Night Caste that was in disguise 24/7. The character was nineteen (I think) and she pretended to be a 40-something male Fire Aspect.<br /> <br /> At no point, in the year that the game went on, did she ever let the other player characters know that she was a Solar or anything. All they knew was her disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds like an amazing concept!<br /> It has a lot of potential for interesting role-playing. Sorry to hear it didn't quite live up to it this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T03:09:50-07:00","id":1243447,"title":"","content":"I'm playing an Eclipse caste with high Larceny. His first encounter with the circle was in disguise as a local, when he hopped down from a tree to acquit one of the other player characters of murder.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T04:04:57-07:00","id":1243452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1242598-your-experience-with-larceny-and-thieves?p=1243346#post1243346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The characters never mad a connection to one-another as it was all based on a lie. The player didn't play his character, he played his character's character. It was basically an extra level of detachment which ensured that the character never cared about much of anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you mean, then. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T07:11:28-07:00","id":1243494,"title":"","content":"At least the Larceny Disguise charms don't last while people are asleep, so it's awkward to be in disguise all the time (unlike Lunars; our Changing Moon used a fake shape for the first two months we knew her, though unlike Kunoichi's player, she didn't pretend to be someone else. She wasn't hiding from us, she was hiding from the Wyld Hunt).<br /> <br /> <br /> I find the disguise charms very useful, and stuff like Seasoned Criminal Method.<br /> Currently I'm following a mad Zenith who's been preaching the apocalypse and gathering a cult (possibly she's a Midnight in disguise). So I just pretended to be a gullible villager, and I've joined her cult while I work out what's going on. It's very useful.<br /> <br /> Lock-opening touch is of course, something that gets used a lot. As is Door-Evading Technique.<br /> Once our Twilight was accused by some local monks of being an anathema. So he let them arrest him, got thrown in prison, and then just wandered off again.<br /> <br /> I haven't seen pickpocketing used much though. Mostly Exalts can get small items they need, and they rarely have to steal keys or something like that. I'm sure it can be useful if you want it to be (and I do like the charm where you nick someone's sword and they don't realise until they try to draw it), but I've not really seen it used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}